  "body": "Slice (c) of #1198. The maintainer asked for this work in his own words (quoted in #1198, 2026-11-12): \"Move / Rotate should be tied to in 3D view control bar floating ontop at the bottom of the viewport.\"\n\nSlice (b), PR #1330, adds the Move mode and the move handles only. No PR and no issue exists for the rotate handles.\n\n**What is wanted**\n- A Rotate mode in the bottom bar of the viewport, next to the Move button of PR #1330.\n- With Rotate on and one shown part selected, the gizmo shows rotation handles (rings, or the axis balls as rotation handles). Decide, and record the decision in `docs/decisions/`.\n- A drag on a handle turns the part about that axis, through the bounding-box centre of the part.\n\n**How it must fit the laws**\n- Everything Is a Command: the drag is an ephemeral preview while the button is down. The release queues ONE undoable command: the same `MoveModel` that the Model page's rotation fields run. No direct field write.\n- Escape during a drag cancels with no history step. A drag that ends at its start angle adds no history step.\n- The rotation changes the placement in the same way as a typed rotation: operations become stale, and stock and fixtures follow as they do now. No new placement path.\n- A handle under the cursor wins the press. Empty space still orbits. The handles keep a constant size on screen.\n- While the user drags, the bar shows the angle.\n- If a new app command is necessary, it gets its MCP tool (AGENTS.md \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\"). The MCP `move_model` tool already sets the rotation.\n- Pin the behaviour in structural and interaction tests, not in PNG snapshots.\n\nDepends on PR #1330 (the Move mode and the `move_drag` module). Stack on that PR, or start after it merges.\n\nDone means: a drag on a rotation handle of the selected part turns the part about the axis, one undo step for each drag, and interaction tests pin the handles, the angle and the undo step.\n\nRefs #1198\n",
